# Opus / token discipline

Prefer small, scoped agent turns. Attach `specs/` (and the current `plans/` slice), not the whole `_notes/` scrapbook.

## When Opus is worth it

Use Opus (or equivalent high-cost reasoning) for:

- Analytics correctness: session/trade-date, expected grid, OHLCV aggregation, rolling VWAP
- DQ engine design, scoring, reconciliation
- Sticky bugs involving timezone, DST, session boundaries, or dual-frequency (`minute` vs `daily`)

Prefer cheaper Cursor models (Composer / Grok) for scaffolding, boilerplate routes, Streamlit chrome, stub tests, and mechanical edits — unless the user has already directed otherwise.

Avoid Opus fast mode unless the user asks for speed; standard rates are enough.

## Context budget

- Attach **only the spec section(s)** needed for the current slice, plus the files being edited
- One concern per chat when possible (e.g. `CMP.*` only, or ingest only, or `/v1/analytics/vwap` only)
- Prefer `@` references to specific paths. Open `_notes/` only when researching, never as implementation law
- If detail still lives only under `_notes/cursor/`, promote it into `specs/` before coding that slice

Doc map for slices (prefer `specs/` once the topic is promoted; until then, research only):

| Slice | Intended spec | Until promoted |
|---|---|---|
| Domain / symbology | (research only; not a v1 product spec) | `_notes/cursor/01-futures-data-primer.md` |
| Bars, VWAP, grid | `specs/analytics-semantics.md` | `_notes/cursor/02-analytics-semantics.md` |
| Schema / SQL | `specs/data-model.md` | `_notes/cursor/03-data-model.md` |
| Rules, score | `specs/dq-rules-and-scoring.md` | `_notes/cursor/04-dq-rules-and-scoring.md` |
| Routes / payloads | `specs/api-contract.md` | `_notes/cursor/05-api-contract.md` |
| Sample facts / oracle tests | `specs/sample-corpus.md` | `_notes/cursor/06-sample-data.md` |
| UI | `specs/loupe-ui-design.md` | — |

## Implementation shape

- Short plan in `plans/` before first app code; then implement one layer or rule family
- Small, testable units; pytest for quality rules and query helpers
- Do not re-litigate locked decisions in `specs/loupe-solution-design.md` unless the user asks
